        "name": "cost-aware-lru-with-weak-freq-and-depth",
        "retention_score": "last_access + 200 * log1p(frequency) + 5 * log1p(depth)",
        "rationale": "Parent (freq-boosted-recency-with-depth-bonus) lost overall despite a huge win on mashqa-train-3-cap2048 because it introduced large regressions on sharegpt (e.g. +9024 extra on sharegpt-1-cap2048, +2640 on sharegpt-1-cap4096 where LRU was already near-zero). Sum across scenarios, not per-scenario wins, is the objective, so avoiding new losses on already-good scenarios matters more than further fixing the biggest loser. Diagnosis: the frequency bonus (400*log1p(freq)) and depth bonus (30*log1p(depth)) are too strong relative to recency. They pull cold-but-fresh blocks below stale-but-frequent/deep blocks, breaking prefix-block ordering. Because blocks form prefixes, a single displaced deep block forces recomputation of everything past it, so preserving strict recency/order alignment (which LRU already does well) is critical. Fix: keep the frequency term (it delivered +10976 on mashqa-3) but halve its weight to 200 so hotness only rescues blocks within a smaller recency window, and cut the depth weight to 5 so depth is only a tie-breaker among similarly-stale candidates rather than a driver. This keeps LRU's ordering behavior on sharegpt (where LRU is already near-optimal) while retaining most of the frequency gains on mashqa. Total should now beat LRU suite-wide: keep mashqa-3 gains, shed most sharegpt regressions. Cheap ops (log1p, mul, add) keep CPU per request well under the 50000us limit."
